Operator: "build the hazard-aware model class" (the forward need from the re-induction work: tu93 L2
stalls because a charging-enemy hazard removes the avatar, which the pure-nav engine can't represent).
Built + 3-skeptic adversarial review (reproduction / causality / scoping); core claim SURVIVES.
Write-up docs/research-notes/hazard-aware-world-model-2026-06-22.md.

- Investigated the tu93 L2 hazard live: colours 8+15 = a charging ENEMY (3x3 colour-8 block + colour-15
  centre, mirror of the avatar) on row 28; stationary until the avatar approaches along its row within
  ~6 cells, then charges to intercept and removes the avatar. Safe path exists (up off its row, then
  right to the goal). Grid-expressible (L2 grid-deterministic, 0.0 nondeterminism / 12012 transitions).
- HazardAwareNavWorldModel (python/carnot/agentic/arc_nav_world_model.py, extends InducedNavWorldModel):
  learns the line-charger FROM TRANSITIONS -- the hazard is the object that MOVES (charges) at the instant
  of death (disambiguates it from the static door) + charge axis/range; goal colour inherited from L1.
  engine predicts avatar-REMOVAL for a lethal move so plan_in_model routes the safe detour. Unit-tested
  (tests/python/test_arc_nav_world_model.py, 6 pass incl. 2 hazard).
- Result (scripts/experiments/experiment_hazard_aware.py, head-to-head, only the model class differs):
  HAZARD_AWARE deepens tu93 L2 + reproduces (reproduced_level=2) on 5/5 seeds; pure-NAV dies on every
  seed. Fit stable [8,15]/row/range6.
- Adversarial confirmations: PARITY-ROBUST (8 fresh envs / reset-8x / fresh-arcade all return L2, no
  [1,2,1,2] toggle despite gotcha #7); CAUSAL (disabling is_lethal collapses to the nav plan + death; a
  nav model refit on the identical data still dies -- the win is solely is_lethal); no hardcoding
  (synthetic colour-6 charger learned correctly).
- Scope (honest, narrowed in review): ONE hazard instance (tu93 line-charger) + 1 synthetic test;
  generality across hazard TYPES not proven. Caveats: death signal self-supplied via the nav suicidal
  plan; charge_range = max(death distances). Not a first solve (tu93 L5 already reproduced via Manhattan
  routing) -- the contribution is the INDUCED world-model + imagination path now handling a hazard level.

